    "result_text": "The full build is green. \n\nI implemented the city-capacity rule following the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions:\n\n- **`CheckOwnerCityCapacity`** \u2014 a new step function that counts existing owners in the request's city (case-insensitive, matching `AssignCustomerCode`'s comparison) and throws when the count is already \u2265 50.\n- **`CityAtCapacityException`** \u2014 a checked exception so it propagates through the `throws` clause to its escalation handler.\n- **`CityAtCapacityExceptionHandler`** + its escalation YAML \u2014 responds **409 Conflict** with a `ProblemDetail`, mirroring the existing duplicate-household handler.\n- Wired the new `checkCityCapacity` step into `owners.POST.yml` after the household check and before `build`, so an over-capacity city is rejected before the owner entity is constructed or saved.\n\n`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 the new `coreRejectsWhenCityAtCapacity` acceptance test (fill a city to 50, expect the 51st to return 409) passes, and `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
